        <p><strong>Legal & Statutory Disclosures:</strong> We may disclose information if required to do so by applicable Indian law, regulation, subpoena, or government order issued by authorized judicial, regulatory, or law enforcement bodies (including the Reserve Bank of India or tax authorities).</p>
      </section>

      <!-- Section 8 -->
      <section id="section-8" class="kitty-pp-card">
        <h2>8. Storage, Security & Android Permissions</h2>
        <p>Swastik Jewels implements multi-layer technical and organizational safeguards:</p>
        <ul class="kitty-bullet-list">
          <li><strong>End-to-End Transport Security (HTTPS):</strong> All client-to-server traffic is transmitted over HTTPS with TLS 1.3 protocol enforcement. Android Network Security Configuration strictly disables cleartext unencrypted HTTP traffic (<code>cleartextTrafficPermitted="false"</code>).</li>
          <li><strong>Database Encryption:</strong> Patron data and KYC records on the backend are protected behind virtual private networks (VPC) with restricted role-based administrative access.</li>
        </ul>

        <h3>Declared Android Permissions & Necessity</h3>
        <div class="kitty-pp-table-container">
          <table class="kitty-pp-table">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th>Permission</th>
                <th>Technical Purpose</th>
                <th>Data Accessed</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <td><code>android.permission.INTERNET</code></td>
                <td>Connecting to the Swastik backend API over secure HTTPS</td>
                <td>Network communication packets</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><code>android.permission.ACCESS_NETWORK_STATE</code></td>
                <td>Detecting online/offline status before initiating payments</td>
                <td>Connection state (WiFi vs Cellular vs Offline)</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><code>android.permission.USE_BIOMETRIC</code></td>
                <td>Optional local biometric verification to unlock the app</td>
                <td>None (Processed strictly on device secure hardware)</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td><code>android.permission.USE_FINGERPRINT</code></td>
                <td>Legacy Android biometric compatibility</td>
                <td>None (Processed strictly on device secure hardware)</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
